<procedure><preliminaryRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The hydraulic power unit is stopped and electrically isolated.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef></reqCondGroup><reqSupportEquips><supportEquipDescrGroup><supportEquipDescr id="seq-0001"><name>Container, oil, 60 L minimum</name><toolRef toolNumber="OIL-CONTAINER-60L"/><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr><supportEquipDescr id="seq-0002"><name>Filter transfer unit, 10 micrometers</name><toolRef toolNumber="FILTER-CART-10UM"/><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr></supportEquipDescrGroup></reqSupportEquips><reqSupplies><supplyDescrGroup><supplyDescr id="sup-0001"><name>Lint-free cloth</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="LINT-FREE-CLOTH" supplyNumberType="sp05"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr><supplyDescr id="sup-0002"><name>Hydraulic oil, HLP 46</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="DIN 51524-2 HLP 46" supplyNumberType="sp02"/><reqQuantity>50 L</reqQuantity></supplyDescr></supplyDescrGroup></reqSupplies><reqSpares><noSpares/></reqSpares><reqSafety><safetyRqmts><warning><warningAndCautionPara>Hydraulic oil can be hot. Let the unit become cool to less than 40 °C before you start this procedure. Hot oil can cause burns.</warningAndCautionPara></warning><warning><warningAndCautionPara>Make sure that the system pressure is 0 bar. Oil under pressure can cause serious injury.</warningAndCautionPara></warning><caution><warningAndCautionPara>Do not let dirt into the reservoir. Dirt in the hydraulic oil can cause damage to the pump and the valves.</warningAndCautionPara></caution></safetyRqmts></reqSafety></preliminaryRqmts><mainProcedure><proceduralStep><title>Drain the oil</title><proceduralStep><para>Put the oil container below the drain plug.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Remove the drain plug. Let all the oil drain into the container.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Clean the magnet of the drain plug with a lint-free cloth. If you find many metal particles, stop and tell your supervisor.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Install the drain plug. Tighten it to 50 N·m.</para></proceduralStep></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><title>Fill the oil</title><proceduralStep><para>Clean the filler-breather cap and the area around it with a lint-free cloth.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Turn the filler-breather cap counterclockwise and remove it.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Connect the outlet hose of the filter transfer unit to the filler opening.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Fill the reservoir with new oil through the filter transfer unit until the oil level is at the maximum mark on the level gauge.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Disconnect the filter transfer unit. Install the filler-breather cap and turn it clockwise until it is tight by hand.</para></proceduralStep></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><title>Bleed and check</title><proceduralStep><para>Start the unit. Operate the actuator through 5 full strokes to bleed air from the system.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Stop the unit. Examine the oil level on the level gauge. If the level is less than the maximum mark, add oil.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Examine the drain plug for leaks.</para></proceduralStep></proceduralStep></mainProcedure><closeRqmts><reqCondGroup><reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The oil level is at the maximum mark, and there are no leaks.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef></reqCondGroup></closeRqmts></procedure>
